 :context
 "Ongoing careful, smaller-batch rollout (capable model + mandatory verification per
  agent) after a prior 18-agent haiku batch had a 61% defect rate. 42+ consecutive
  agents on this stricter protocol had succeeded before this one. Built from
  cloud-itonami-isic-0113 (growing of vegetables and melons, roots and tubers) as
  the module-structure template, with clojure -M:test independently re-run from
  fresh clones before and after push. The kotoba-lang/industry registry entry for
  \"0119\" was independently re-verified (fresh clone) before any implementation
  work to confirm id/name match (several prior agents in this fleet had mislabeled
  their assigned ISIC class, e.g. 0892 assumed=salt actually=peat, 0144
  assumed=swine actually=sheep-goats): {:id \"0119\" :name \"Growing of other
  non-perennial crops\" ...} genuinely confirmed, no mismatch. gh api confirmed no
  prior repository existed at either cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isic-0119 or the
  stale gftdcojp/cloud-itonami-A0119 placeholder (404)."

 :scope-exclusions
 ["direct field-equipment operation (farmer's exclusive authority)"
  "finalizing a pesticide-application decision (agronomist/farmer authority)"
  "agronomic decision authority -- what/when/how much to plant, spray, irrigate, harvest (remains human authority)"]

 :decision
 "Implement cloud-itonami-isic-0119 with Governor, Facts, Registry, Store, Advisor,
  Phase, Operation, Sim (mirrors cloud-itonami-isic-0113 module-for-module,
  namespace othercropops.* in place of vegops.*, no additional domain-specific
  Governor gate -- the task's domain design specified the same closed op-allowlist
  and hard-invariant shape as 0113 with no extra check):
  - Governor (FieldOperationsGovernor): 5 hard checks (field-not-registered,
    no-execution, equipment-or-pesticide-decision-blocked, op-not-allowed,
    field-record-invalid) + 3 escalation gates (always-escalate crop-health
    concern, cost-threshold supply orders, low confidence < 0.7)
  - Facts: supply categories with cost thresholds (seed/fertilizer/equipment),
    other-non-perennial-crop classification (fodder-corn/alfalfa/clover/
    forage-kale/cut-flower/ornamental-plant/flower-seed/vegetable-seed --
    excludes cereals [0111], rice [0112], sugar cane/beet [0114], tobacco [0115],
    fibre crops [0116], grapes [0121])
  - Registry: independent pure predicates (cost-exceeds-threshold?,
    acreage-non-positive?, confidence-below-floor?)
  - Store: Store protocol + MemStore (registered-field lookup)
  - Advisor: Advisor protocol + MockAdvisor (4 ops)
  - Phase: 0->3 rollout gate
  - Operation: composes advisor -> governor -> phase-gate (langgraph-clj wiring
    deferred, matching 0113's own stub)
  - Sim: demo runner with a working -main, verified end-to-end
  - Operations: log-field-record, schedule-field-operation,
    flag-crop-health-concern, order-supplies (closed allowlist, :effect :propose)
  - Tests: 30 tests / 102 assertions (facts, governor, phase, registry, store), all
    green (3 more assertions than 0113's 99 because facts_test adds explicit
    out-of-scope checks for sugar-cane/beet [0114], tobacco [0115], and fibre
    crops [0116] on top of 0113's cereals/rice/grapes exclusion checks)
  - All .cljc (portable, no JVM interop), AGPL-3.0-or-later
  - README/business-model/operator-guide describe the real API"

 :consequences
 {:positive
  ["Other-non-perennial-crop growing (0119) now genuinely implemented and fully
    tested"
   "Scope boundaries (field-equipment operation, pesticide-application decisions)
